{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>Seasoned (ממולח).</b> They would put salt in the incense, and this is what the Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: 'Sodomite salt, a quarter.' And it is possible to interpret ממולח as 'mixed,' as in its Targum — that one mixes it well so that the spices not be discernible; and therefore men of the sea are called מלחים because they mix the waters with their rowing, and it is from the language of (Ezekiel 27:9) ״מלחיך וחובליך״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:05:46.842666830Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}